# Data Source: identitynow_notification_template

Use this data source to look up a custom notification template by ID, or by key, medium and locale. Only templates customized in the tenant are found, not the default templates.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile .ExampleFile }}

## Arguments Reference

Set either `id`, or all of `key`, `medium` and `locale`:

* `id` - (Optional) Template ID.
* `key` - (Optional) Template key.
* `medium` - (Optional) Message medium: `EMAIL`, `SLACK` or `TEAMS`.
* `locale` - (Optional) Locale as a BCP 47 language tag, e.g. `en`.

## Attributes Reference

* `name` - Template name.
* `subject` - Subject line.
* `body` - Message body.
* `header` - Deprecated header.
* `footer` - Deprecated footer.
* `from` - "From:" address.
* `reply_to` - "Reply To" address.
* `description` - Template description.
* `slack_template_json` - Slack template as a JSON object, without empty values.
* `teams_template_json` - Microsoft Teams template as a JSON object, without empty values.
* `created` - Creation date.
* `modified` - Last modification date.
